# Audio manager
Simple app to control audio in linux

## Make sure installed
```bash
sudo apt install libgtk-4-dev libgtk-4-1 pulseaudio-utils
```
- `libgtk-4-dev` - GTK4 development files
- `libgtk-4-1` - GTK4 runtime
- `pulseaudio-utils` - PulseAudio utils

## compile command
```bash
gcc $(pkg-config --cflags gtk4 libpulse libpulse-mainloop-glib) src/main.c src/window.c src/callbacks.c src/process.c src/audio.c -o bam $(pkg-config --libs gtk4 libpulse libpulse-mainloop-glib) -lX11
```

## .desktop
In the file ending with `.desktop` replace `Exec` & `Icon` with the correct path
Make copy of the file ending with `.desktop` to `/home/<your user>/.local/share/applications` as is
To see immediate result run: `update-desktop-database ~/.local/share/applications/`
